<Legal title="Privacy Policy" description="How Aptora handles your resume, job description and account data — privacy by design." path="/privacy">
  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p class="lg-updated">Last updated: September 2026</p>

  <p>Your privacy matters. This policy explains what Aptora, by Enally, collects and how it is used and protected. Aptora handles resumes and job descriptions, which can contain personal details such as your name, contact information, and work history.</p>

  <h2>What we process</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Resume and job description content</strong> you provide, to generate and tailor your document.</li>
    <li><strong>Generated PDFs</strong>, stored temporarily so you can download them.</li>
    <li><strong>An anonymous session identifier</strong> stored in a secure cookie, used to keep your work private to you and to count free usage. It is not derived from your email or IP.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How your data is protected</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Your files and inputs are scoped to your session — only your session can access them.</li>
    <li>Uploaded inputs and generated files are <strong>temporary</strong> and are automatically deleted after they expire.</li>
    <li>We do not sell your personal data.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Temporary file hosting</h2>
  <p>Generated PDFs may be hosted on a short-lived link so you can download them, and are removed after expiry. Do not treat these links as private or permanent.</p>

  <h2>AI processing</h2>
  <p>To tailor and analyze your resume, content is sent to a third-party AI provider for processing. It is used only to produce your result and is not used to identify you.</p>

  <h2>Your choices</h2>
  <p>You can delete saved inputs from the "My files" area at any time. Clearing your session removes access to your temporary data.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Privacy questions? Reach us through the contact options in the app's Help menu.</p>
</Legal>
